    {
        "content": "<p>Usually it's that the tactics are viewing the terms at different transparency modes, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode</a>. You can see these in what <code>exact</code> is doing:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- exact accepts all 3 defeq's</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ...but not at all transparencies</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double_abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The tactics <code>simp</code> and <code>rw</code> both use <code>reducible</code> transparency, so they will not see through some of these defeqs. They do not match up with <code>with_reducible exact h</code> exactly though, because they also have additional optimizations to avoid having to try to unify every possible pair of (lemma, subtem). In particular, <code>simp</code> uses a discrimination tree (see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.DiscrTree#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.DiscrTree</a>), and <code>rw</code> only checks subterms with the same <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.HeadIndex#doc\">docs#Lean.HeadIndex</a> (see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.kabstract#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.kabstract</a>).</p>",
        "id": 597340119,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779569108
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are lots of levels of equality yes. There is propositional equality (where <code>rfl</code> doesn't work) and then there are lots of kinds of definitional equality, and these are linearly ordered; there is \"<code>rfl</code> works\" (which is the weakest) and then there are things like \"<code>with_reducible rfl</code>\" works and \"<code>with_reducible_and_instances rfl</code> works\"; what controls this is something called transparency. Typically a <code>rfl</code> in a certain context will run at a certain transparency. For example typeclass inference will work at instance transparency, <code>rw</code> will try <code>rfl</code> at the end with reducible transparency, but if you run the <code>rfl</code> tactic in a proof then it will run aggressively, i.e. keep unfolding things (the transparency is controlling exactly what gets unfolded, so for example <code>abbrev</code> and <code>def</code> are treated differently, <code>abbrev</code> will unfold at reducible transparency but not <code>def</code>). And then at the very top there is syntactic equality, which means \"literally the same term\" (i.e. it sees through notation but nothing else). <code>rw</code> and <code>simp</code> match terms either up to syntactic equality or reducible definitional equality (I forgot); <code>exact</code> and <code>apply</code> and <code>refine</code> work up to aggressive definitional equality so they will unfold anything.</p>",
        "id": 597340241,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779569230
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>from the docs you sent </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The levels form a linear order: none &lt; reducible &lt; instances &lt; default &lt; all.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is indeed sounds like the order I was looking for. Thanks, will read up more! Will pressure test it whether different tactics respect it uniformly - i.e. tactic X unfolds everything up to transparency Y.</p>",
        "id": 597340489,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779569488
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode</a> is a nice read about it</p>",
        "id": 597340863,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779569887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.ReducibilityStatus#doc\">docs#Lean.ReducibilityStatus</a></p>",
        "id": 597340970,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779569986
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, a bit surprised that <a href=\"https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/\">https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/</a> doesn't mention anything about this (unless I missed it?), given how easy one can run into differences here - like deciding whether to use <code>abbrev</code> vs <code>def</code> in their first non-trivial lean definitions.</p>",
        "id": 597340973,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779569989
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The docs linked are great above are great! I already learned a lot by reading them. Sadly they are a bit undiscoverable (unless one asks on zulip and is pointed to them.)</p>",
        "id": 597341478,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779570474
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>Historically, Lean bumped transparency to <code>.[default](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/MetaTypes.html#Lean.instInhabitedNameGenerator.default)</code> for implicit arguments</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I just learned that the unfolding degree depends not only on the tactic, but also on the position of the argument.</p>",
        "id": 597341572,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779570578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not the position (is it?), it's the binder type (<code>{x}</code> v (x)`). Leo's talk in Portugal on Wednesday demoed this phenomenon.</p>",
        "id": 597344741,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779574201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, I should have said the type of argument - implicit or explicit not position. Now I wonder if it is how it is declared as a parameter or how it is passed as an argument - I.e. which rules does f (x:=x) follow - implicit parameter passed as explicit argument.</p>",
        "id": 597348309,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779577199
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well this special behavior for implicit variables was dropped in v4.29 so I think the answer now is all (non-instance) parameters are treated the same<br>\n(unless you <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> to revert to the old behavior)</p>",
        "id": 597348528,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779577417
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"488971\">Rado Kirov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/levels.20of.20equality.20between.20syntactic.20and.20definitional/near/597340973\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, a bit surprised that <a href=\"https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/\">https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/</a> doesn't mention anything about this (unless I missed it?), given how easy one can run into differences here - like deciding whether to use <code>abbrev</code> vs <code>def</code> in their first non-trivial lean definitions.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed this may be because , as you noted , in the past there was a promotion of arguments in tactics. So it wasn’t as important for users , until this change of course. </p>\n<p>Perhaps some of the introductory texts should add in a little bit about this after the default transparency change.</p>",
        "id": 597366797,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1779594238
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I kept playing with this until I got this #mfe for a <code>respectTransparency</code> change. I kept asking Claude, who could both come up some interesting directions and also completely wrong explanations that I kept invalidating with examples in the playground.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- implicit param</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- three ways to write it, but they seem to act equivalently</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- explcit param</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myIdEx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fooEx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myIdEx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backward</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respectTransparency</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- only fails with respectTransparency true (which is default in v4.30)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">foo'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">foo''</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- always fails</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myIdEx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">fooEx</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To answer my question above - it is about whether the param was implicit at the declaration, not whether it was bound to an argument with @ or (x := y).</p>",
        "id": 597367246,
        "sender_full_name": "Rado Kirov",
        "timestamp": 1779594665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>whether or not the parameter is bound with an <code>@</code> or a <code>(x := y)</code> is not reflected in the final expression, so it couldn't possibly depend on that</p>",
        "id": 597389956,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779619045
    }
]